      <article>
        <h1>A kind of fish taco</h1>
        <p><em>Crunchy, zesty, and unapologetically inauthentic – because tacos don't need passports.</em></p>
        <p class="meta">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-people-group"></i> 4
        </p>
        <details open>
          <summary>📋 Ingredients</summary>
          <ul class="content">
            <li><strong>Fish:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>2 white fish fillets (cod/hake)</li>
                <li>1 tbsp spicy paprika</li>
                <li>½ tsp cumin</li>
                <li>½ tsp chilli flakes</li>
                <li>1 lime (juiced)</li>
                <li>Salt & pepper</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Toppings:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>1 avocado</li>
                <li>¼ cabbage, shredded</li>
                <li>1 carrot, grated</li>
                <li>1 tomato, diced</li>
                <li>½ onion, finely chopped</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Extras:</strong>
              <ul>
                <li>Tortillas</li>
                <li>Hot sauce</li>
                <li>Oil/vinegar (for coleslaw)</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>🍳 Method</summary>
          <div class="content">
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Prep:</strong>
                <ul>
                  <li>Chop onion/tomato, smash avocado, shred cabbage, grate carrot.</li>
                  <li>Mix spices with lime juice to form a paste (add juice slowly).</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Fish:</strong>
                <ul>
                  <li>Coat fish in spice paste.</li>
                  <li><strong>Air fryer:</strong> 180°C for 12-15 mins (fresh) or 18-20 mins (frozen).</li>
                  <li><em>TIP:</em> "Frozen works, but fresh absorbs more flavor. Fork-test for flakiness."</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Sides:</strong>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Guac:</strong> Smash avocado + lime + salt + chilli flakes + onion/tomato.</li>
                  <li><strong>Slaw:</strong> Mix cabbage, carrot, onion + salt, pepper, oil, vinegar.</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Serve:</strong>
                <ul>
                  <li>Heat tortillas in dry pan (30 secs/side).</li>
                  <li>Flake fish into chunks, load up tacos with slaw/guac.</li>
                  <li>Drown in hot sauce (optional but recommended).</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>💰 Budget Notes</summary>
